    "event": "Dense Fog Advisory",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Goodland KS",
    "headline": "Dense Fog Advisory issued November 13 at 7:41AM MST until November 13 at 10:00AM MST by NWS Goodland KS",
    "description": "* WHAT...Visibility less than one quarter mile in dense fog.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central Colorado, northwest and west\ncentral Kansas, and southwest Nebraska.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 AM MST /11 AM CST/ this morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hazardous driving conditions.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Locations with temperatures in the upper 20s\nand lower 30s, such as McCook and Oberlin, can expect dense\nfreezing fog.",
    "instruction": "Be prepared for rapid reductions in visibility. Drivers are urged to\nslow down, use low beam headlights and leave plenty of following\ndistance. Exercise caution, especially at intersections and highway\nonramps and offramps, where accidents are more likely to occur.",
    "response": "Execute",
    "note": null,
